    "body": "fix on issue/2227-klartext-contours - PR #4468 - pinned by klartext_rnd_rounds_a_right_angle_with_its_own_feed, klartext_chf_and_rnd_chain_on_right_turns, klartext_rnd_on_an_obtuse_corner_is_tangent_to_both_lines, klartext_rnd_between_l_and_lp_lines, klartext_rnd_on_the_first_move_of_a_section_starts_at_the_line_start, klartext_transition_elements_refuse_what_is_not_exact, klartext_lp_reaches_polar_points_about_the_pole, klartext_cp_arcs_about_the_pole_in_both_directions, klartext_cp_with_iz_is_a_helix_split_into_quarter_turns, klartext_polar_blocks_refuse_what_is_not_exact, klartext_seeded_mutations_of_the_contour_never_panic - merges at the next cut\n\nThis PR is the third slice (`Refs #2227`), stacked on #4460. The reader now reads RND and CHF between two straight lines, polar LP and CP about CC, and the CP helix. These items stay open on this issue:\n- `RND` / `CHF` next to an arc (`C`, `CR`, `CT`, `CP`).\n- `CTP` (tangential polar arc).\n- `APPR` / `DEP`.\n- Radius compensation `RL` / `RR`.\n- `LBL` / `CALL LBL` subprogram calls.\n- Inch programs.\n- Rigid tapping with a left-hand thread (negative Q239).\nThe reader refuses each of them by name, with the line and the block number.\n",
